it</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Hartsky</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Role of alveolar macrophage chemotaxis in pulmonary clearance responses to inhaled particles: comparisons among rodent species</article-title><source>Microsc Res Tech</source><year>1993</year><volume>26</volume><fpage>412</fpage><lpage>422</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8286787</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/jemt.1070260509</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Godfrey</surname><given-names>RW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human airway epithelial tight junctions</article-title><source>Microsc Res Tech</source><year>1997</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>488</fpage><lpage>499</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9376652</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/(SICI)1097-0029(19970901)38:5&#x0003c;488::AID-JEMT5&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-E</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maina</surname><given-names>JN</given-names></name><name><surname>West</surname><given-names>JB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Thin and strong! The bioengineering dilemma in the structural and functional design of the blood-gas barrier</article-title><source>Physiol Rev</source><year>2005</year><volume>85</volume><fpage>811</fpage><lpage>844</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15987796</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1152/physrev.00022.2004</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holt</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name><name><surname>Schon-Hergard</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name><name><surname>McMenamin</surname><given-names>PG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Dendritic cells in the respiratory tract</article-title><source>Int Rev Immunol</source><year>1990</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>139</fpage><lpage>149</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2152499</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.3109/08830189009056625</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schulz</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Brand</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Heyder</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Gehr P, Heyder J</surname></name></person-group><article-title>Particle deposition in the respiratory tract</article-title><source>Particle-lung interactions</source><year>2000</year><publisher-name>New York Basel: Marcel Dekker</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kendall</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Tetley</surname><given-names>TD</given-names></name><name><surname>Wigzell</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Hutton</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Nieuwenhuijsen</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Luckham</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lung lining liquid modifies PM<sub>2.5 </sub>in favour of particle aggregation: a protective mechanism</article-title><source>Am J Physiol Lung Cell Mol Physiol</source><year>2002</year><volume>282</volume><fpage>L109</fpage><lpage>L114</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11741822</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Geiser</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Rothen-Rutishauser</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Kapp</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Sch&#x